## Executive Summary

Claude Fable 5.1 is Anthropic's general-availability Mythos-tier model released September 1, 2026, designed for long-running agentic workflows, coding, and knowledge work. It shares the same underlying model as Claude Mythos 5.1 but with additional safeguards for general availability. The model features a massive 1M token context window, competitive pricing ($10/$50 per 1M tokens), and strong performance across agentic coding and reasoning benchmarks. Fable 5.1 ranks #1 on the RSI Index (35.03%), leading the previous leader Claude Opus 5 (32.10%) while costing 21% less per task. It offers strong multimodal capabilities, comprehensive tool support, and excellent cost efficiency when considering prompt caching discounts.

---

## Model Identity and Background

**Developer:** Anthropic
**Release Date:** September 1, 2026
**Series:** Claude Fable (Fable 5.1)
**Predecessor:** Claude Fable 5 (June 2026)
**Successor:** Claude Opus 5.5 (September 22, 2026)
**License:** Proprietary
**Context Window:** 1,000,000 tokens
**Max Output:** 128,000 tokens

Claude Fable 5.1 is the latest general-availability model in Anthropic's Claude family, positioned as the company's strongest option for long-running agentic work, coding, and knowledge work. It shares its underlying model architecture with Claude Mythos 5.1 but includes additional safety guardrails and more permissive access for general users. Fable 5.1 represents a significant advancement in Anthropic's capabilities, particularly in agentic coding workflows, long-context reasoning, and complex knowledge work.

